        <mxCell id="note" value="µP circles mark points the microcontroller sets or reads (spec: sensor readings, references and the 60 Hz drive are under processor control). Spec col. 5: limiter 68 clamps the inner-loop output 38; together with the knock sensor 64/66 (PZT/microphone, back-EMF or current analyzer detecting OVERSTROKES) it keeps the cooler from being overdriven, e.g. at start-up; with thermistor 60/62 it limits power when the cooler gets too hot. Multiplier 70 amplitude-modulates the 60 Hz drive with limiter output 72. PD amp 32 inputs: 36 (primary), reference 74, cold finger 33. See analysis/OVERSTROKE.md." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
